==Trivia==
*Squire Rel's Japanese name, Rissuntumī (リッスントゥミー), literally translates to "Listen-to-me", but is also a pun on 栗鼠 ''risu'' (squirrel).
*Squire Rel's description references the English conversation schools commonly found outside train stations across Japan. None of them have a squirrel as a mascot however, although arguably the most infamous chain did have a rabbit-like thing.
*Prior to [[Version 14.7 Update|Version 14.7]], Squire Rel's description was:
<pre>
She speaks an old English dialect (?).
No, seriously, it sounds like English, but
it's too hard understand what she says.
Works at the English school near the station.
</pre>
*[[Sir Rel]]'s Japanese description implies that he learned English from Squire Rel via time travel, but can't speak it well enough for anyone to understand because Squire Rel taught him the same dialect that makes them incomprehensible to others.
*Since [[Revival of Origin]] features a [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]], the stage's Squire Rel or Sir Rel may represent [[wikipedia:Ratatoskr|Ratatoskr]], a squirrel in Norse mythology who runs up and down the world tree [[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]] to carry messages between the eagle perched atop the tree and [[wikipedia:Nidhogg|Nidhogg]], the serpent below the tree.
*Sir Rel may have been inspired by the 40,000% Squire Rels from [[Apple Bobbing Ocean]], which deal only 500 less damage per hit than a 100% Sir Rel (12,500 > 12,000).
*Not counting [[Lord Gravey]] and [[Miss Haka]], Squire Rel has the fewest variants of all [[Empire of Cats]] enemies, with only one, that being Sir Rel.

